  "presentation_summary": [
    "Healthy 26-year-old woman developed fever, about 10 watery stools, lower abdominal pain, bloody stools, and vomiting after eating raw spring rolls at a restaurant.",
    "She received levofloxacin 500 mg/day for 3 days for presumed infectious gastroenteritis before referral.",
    "On illness day 7, stool culture from the first hospital detected EHEC O157 positive for verotoxins 1 and 2; diarrhea was improving and admission vitals were stable except tachycardia.",
    "Despite few subjective symptoms, delayed HUS developed on illness day 11 with thrombocytopenia, hemolytic anemia, high LDH, low haptoglobin, fragmented RBCs, proteinuria/hematuria, and creatinine rise.",
    "She was treated with IV extracellular fluid and recovered by outpatient follow-up."
  ],
